Sure, if you want to run it you can use the attached model files, and data saved as an RDS file. I should note that to make the two models match I had to alter the originally linked Stan model. In particular I used the 'ones trick' <http://users.aims.ac.za/~mackay/BUGS/Manuals/Tricks.html#SpecifyingANewSamplingDistribution>, and did some preprocessing of the data since JAGS doesn't have a transformed parameter section. This is mostly because JAGS can't do the while loop (at least as far as I could find), so I had to work around that. Also note that this requires JAGS 4.2.0 and rjags 4.4. The rjags version isn't up on CRAN but can be found here:  https://sourceforge.net/projects/mcmc-jags/files/rjags/4/ and installed manually.  I was really curious to see the differences on identical parameterizations, hence all the extra leg work. The Stan model runs about the same as the original.

Thanks for taking a look.

