Hi,

following Bob's instruction you should get this implementation of the ODE

 functions {
    real[] diff_y(real t,
                  real[] y,
                  real[] theta,
                  real[] x_r,
                  int[] x_i) {

      real dydt;
      dydt <- 2*pi()/theta[1] * (1+theta[2]*cos(y))^2 / (1-theta[2]^2)^1.5;
      return dydt;
    }
  }

Here theta[1] and theta[2] are your para[0] and para[1] respectively, so you need to reassign.
Then use the call

y <- integrate_ode(diff_y, y0, t0, ts, theta, x_r, x_i);

Does this work for you?
Liza.

