As a minimal example

  template<typename Derived> Derived operator()(
      const Eigen::Matrix<Derived, Eigen::Dynamic, 1>& theta) const {

    return sin(theta(0)*theta(1));
  }

This works with numeric differentiation
stan::math::finite_diff_hessian(f, theta, cost, G, H );

as you recommended, but doesn't compile with hessian
stan::math::hessian(f, theta, cost, G, H);

error: no matching function for call to ‘sin(stan::math::fvar<stan::math::var>)’

I just want to confirm that this is expected.

Thanks!

