That should give you the same answer as

> vector[hn] mu;
> mudev~normal(0,1);
> mu<-hmu+mudev*hsd;

mu ~ normal(hmu, hsd);

assuming you declare mu as an unconstrained parameter.

You shouldn't need that lower=0.001 for scales in Stan.  If you
do need it, it's indicating a problem with your model and will
lead to computational problems trying to sample near the boundary.
We also don't recommend upper-bounding scale parameters.

- Bob

