Hi Terrance,

We don't have R-style replacement functions (not sure if that's on Bob's long-term to-do list for the language or not), so you can't do something like

block(A, ...) <- B;

However, recent versions of Stan do allow for much more flexibility with indexing (including for assignment), so I think you should be able to do things like

A[i:j, k:l] <- B; // i,j,k,l integers
A[row_ids, col_ids] <- B; //row_ids, col_ids integer arrays

that weren't previously possible. Hope that helps,

Jonah

