I think the problem is here. The support of pdf is [0,theta], so theta has to be larger than the largest observed value of x. So, at least, those constraints should be added to the model (and the priors should be changed accordingly). Also, it's probably a good idea to write down the log-density directly and avoid those pow() calculations, that way it should be more numerically stable and maybe a bit more efficient as well.

