I think at least one of the issues is how objects of the type "vector" play with objects of the type "ordered", the latter of which are supposed to just be vector of ordered scalars (right?).

I notice huge differences in the simulated data output from the stan model if I declare "y" to be a vector (it's totally messed up, no idea why it delivers these values) versus an "ordered" type, which works pretty well. But why do they give such different output? What is "ordered" doing exactly? And why does having a line like:

